  "overview": "**Tabler UI** is a light-first design system anchored on `#fff` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (19.7:1 contrast) and `#066fd1` brand accent.\n\nTypography centers cleanly on `System UI` (80px display down to 16px body), unified by `12px` base corner radius and subtle shadow elevation.\n\nMaintained by **Tabler**. Source: published token package (https://tabler.io), package `@tabler/core`. Inventory: **91** colors, **109** typography steps, and **25** documented components (MIT license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 25 component tokens with documented paddings: `0.5rem 1rem`, `0.25rem 0.5rem`, `0`, `0.5625rem 1rem`, `2px`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `rgb(231, 240, 249)` cards; separate sibling sections using `rgb(72.836712561%, 72.836712561%, 72.836712561%)` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Layered Shadow Model**: Uses documented shadows (`0 1px 2px 0 color-mix(in oklab, light-dark(rgba(18, 18, 23, 0.4), #000) 12.5%, transparent)`) paired with `rgb(72.836712561%, 72.836712561%, 72.836712561%)` borders for elevated overlays.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `#066fd1` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#fff` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `rgba(153, 159, 164, 1)` secondary labels.\n- Use `#066fd1` with `#f7f7f8` text (4.7:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `System UI` headings with `System UI` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `12px` base geometry across inputs and buttons (12px on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `rgb(231, 240, 249)` surface shifts and `rgb(72.836712561%, 72.836712561%, 72.836712561%)` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `12px` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `input` fields and secondary buttons."
}
